  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;Principle\r\nof Development&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development would result in the creation of a standalone 1-bedroom,\r\n1-person dwelling on a garage and/or backland site within an area with a Public\r\nTransport Accessibility Level (PTAL) of 2. The proposal would not accord with\r\nthe Council&#x27;s housing mix objectives and has failed to demonstrate a\r\ncomprehensive approach to the development potential of the wider surrounding\r\nland. The development would therefore represent the piecemeal redevelopment of\r\nan individual garage and/or backland plot, contrary to the objectives of\r\ncomprehensive development and effective use of land. As such, the proposal\r\nconflicts with Policies HO1 and GR10 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021–2041),\r\nPolicies H1 and H2 of the London Plan (2021), and the objectives of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;\r\nmso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;Future\r\nOccupier Amenity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed dwelling would fail to provide a high-quality standard of\r\naccommodation for future occupiers by reason of its constrained internal\r\narrangement, lack of demonstrated internal storage provision, failure to\r\ndemonstrate compliance with the minimum floor-to-ceiling height expectations of\r\nLondon Plan Policy D6, limited outlook, inadequate private outdoor amenity\r\nspace and the absence of sufficient information to demonstrate satisfactory\r\nresidential living conditions within the converted garage structure. The\r\nproposal would therefore fail to provide a high standard of residential\r\naccommodation and would be contrary to Paragraph 135 of the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework, Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1(C) of the\r\nHarrow Local Plan (2021–2041).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
  "decision": "Refused",
